course: dictionary
lesson: 312
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and anchor is one of them. You can work out which meaning you need by reading the words around it. «The ship dropped anchor in the bay» tells you the anchor is a heavy hook, because ships and bays are about water and boats.
explain: Now read this: «The news anchor smiled at the camera.» There is no ship here. The words news and camera give the clue: an anchor can be the main person who presents a TV news programme. Always ask which meaning fits, then test it in the sentence.
explain: Anchor can also be a doing word. «They anchored the tent with heavy stones» means they fixed it firmly so the wind could not blow it away. Check your choice by swapping in your own meaning and reading the sentence again.
fact: An anchor is a heavy object on a chain or rope, dropped from a boat to stop it drifting.
fact: To anchor means to stop a boat with an anchor, or to fix something firmly so it cannot move.
fact: A news anchor is the main person who presents a TV news programme.
fact: In a relay race or tug of war, the anchor is the strongest team member, who goes last.
fact: «Drop anchor» means let the anchor down, and «weigh anchor» means pull it up to leave.
exercise: «The ship dropped anchor in the bay.» What does anchor mean here? | A person who reads the news on TV | The strongest runner who goes last | *A heavy hook on a chain that stops a boat | A big wooden box for tools
exercise: «The news anchor smiled at the camera.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | *The main person who presents a TV news programme | A heavy hook for a boat | The last runner in a relay race | A tall tree in the park
exercise: «They anchored the tent with heavy stones.» What does anchored mean here? | Dug a hole in the sand | Swam fast across a lake | Sang loudly at a party | *Fixed firmly so it cannot move
test: In tug of war, Sam was picked as the anchor because he was the strongest. What does anchor mean here? | A referee who blows the whistle | The first person to pull the rope | *The strongest team member, who goes last | A heavy boat hook
test: «The sailors had to weigh anchor before the storm came.» What does weigh anchor mean? | Paint the anchor red | Count how heavy the anchor is | *Pull the anchor up to leave | Drop the anchor into the sea
exam: «Tie the bookshelf to the wall so it is anchored and cannot fall.» What does anchored mean? | Sold to a shop | *Firmly fixed so it cannot move | Lifted high into the air | Painted with bright colours
